\ref{item:dissineq3}$\Rightarrow$\ref{item:dissineq1}:
Let $(x(\cdot),u(\cdot),y(\cdot))$ be a~classical trajectory of \eqref{eq:ODEnode} on $[0,T]$. Consider a `mollifier sequence' $(\alpha_n)_{n\in{\mathbb{N}}}$ in $\mathrm{C}^\infty({\mathbb{R}})$, see Definition~\ref{def:molli}, and consider the 
convolutions 
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
x_n(\cdot)&=(\alpha_n\ast x)(\cdot):[0,T]\to\mathcal{X},\\
u_n(\cdot)&=(\alpha_n\ast u)(\cdot):[0,T]\to\mathcal{U}, \\
y_n(\cdot)&=(\alpha_n\ast y)(\cdot) :[0,T]\to\mathcal{Y}.    
\end{aligned}\label{eq:conxuy}
\end{equation}
Then Lemma~\ref{lem:mollconv} yields that these functions are all infinitely often differentiable. Further, the same lemma implies that the restriction of  $(x_n(\cdot),u_n(\cdot),y_n(\cdot))$ to $[0,T-1/n]$ is a~classical trajectory of \eqref{eq:ODEnode} on $[0,T-1/n]$.
Then Lemma~\ref{lem:smoothsol}
yields that the restrictions of $x_n(\cdot)$ and $\left(\begin{smallmatrix}x_n(\cdot)\\u_n(\cdot)\end{smallmatrix}\right)$ to $[0,T-1/n]$ are 
in $\mathrm{C}^{1}([0,t];\mathcal{V})$ and $\mathrm{C}([0,t];\mathcal{W})$, resp. An application of Proposition~\ref{prop:Storsmooth} leads to continuous differentiability of $\scprod{\widetilde{P}x_n(\cdot)}{x_n(\cdot)}_{\mathcal{V} 
  \setcounter{i}{1} 
  \striche={\ast} 
  \loop 
  \ifnum\value{i}<1 
  \striche=\expandafter{\the\expandafter\striche\ast} 
  \stepcounter{i} 
  \repeat 
  ^{\the\striche} 
,\mathcal{V}}$, and for all $t\in[0,T-1/n]$,
\[
\tfrac{\text{\normalfont d}}{\text{\normalfont d}t}\scprod{\widetilde{P}x_n(t)}{x_n(t)}=2\operatorname{Re}\scprod*{\widetilde{P}x_n(t)}{A\&B\left(\begin{smallmatrix}{x}_n(t)\\u_n(t)\end{smallmatrix}\right)}_{\mathcal{V} 
